<title>TURKEY: Turk Petkim '96 net profits rise 7.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Petkim '96 net profits rise 7.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   8,148.98  vs   7,576.27</p>
<p>    Net profit		   24,446.95  vs  22,728.80</p>
<p>    Net sales		    72,390.06  vs  55,149.66</p>
<p>    Operating profit	   16,557.14  vs  23,230.62</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	 30,118.25  vs  14,993.03</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   479.41  vs     765.51</p>
<p>    Extraordinary expense     1,749.05  vs   1,362.23</p>
<p>    Total debts		  24,378.05  vs  19,232.02</p>
<p>    Equity			 97,685.30  vs  66,016.77</p>
<p>    Capital			 3,000.00  vs   3,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's largely state-owned petrochemicals giant Petkim - Petrokimya Holding A.S. is slated for privatisation, with 96 percent of its shares held by the privatisation administration OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 1996 wholesale inflation of 84.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
